[Verification "Stockfish 18 NNUE checked; see accompanying report"]
[IntendedResult "win"]

{ Both sides have a runner, and his h pawn is racing for h1. Find the move that wins the race. } 4. a6 { Your a pawn runs on. A new queen on a8 stands on the same long diagonal as h1. [%cal Ga5a6,Ga8h1] } (4. axb6 { Taking the pawn moves your runner to the b column. } 4... h3 5. b7 h2 6. b8=Q h1=Q { Drawn: you both have a queen, and yours on b8 cannot see h1, so his queen arrived safely. [%csl Rh1] }) (4. Ka4 { King to a4 stops to fight his b pawn. } 4... bxa5 5. Kxa5 Kg6 6. Kb4 h3 { Lost: your a pawn is gone, and his h pawn has a clear road to h1. [%csl Rh1] }) (4. Kb4 { King to b4 spends the move your pawn needed. } 4... bxa5+ 5. Kxa5 Kg6 6. Kb4 h3 { Lost: the pawns traded on a5, you have no runner left, and his h pawn is two steps from h1. [%csl Rh3] }) (4. Kc4 { King to c4 goes the long way round his b pawn. } 4... bxa5 5. Kb5 Kf6 6. Kxa5 Ke5 { Lost: you won his b pawn back, but your a pawn was taken first, and his h pawn still runs free. [%csl Rh4] }) 4... h3 { He races his h pawn on. } 5. a7 { Your pawn is on a7, one step from a8, and a8 sees h1 down the long diagonal. [%cal Ga6a7,Ga8h1] } (5. Kc4 { King to c4 costs the move the race cannot spare. } 5... h2 6. a7 h1=Q 7. Kb5 Qa8 { Lost: his queen was born first, on h1, and now she stands on a8 in front of your pawn. [%csl Ra8] }) (5. Ka3 { King to a3 walks when the pawn should run. } 5... h2 6. Ka4 Kf7 7. Kb5 h1=Q { Lost: his pawn queened on h1 while your king walked, and your a pawn is still on a6. [%csl Rh1] }) (5. Kb4 { King to b4 goes after the b pawn. } 5... h2 6. Kb5 Kf6 7. Kxb6 h1=Q { Lost: your king took the b pawn, but his pawn queened on h1 in the time it took. [%csl Rh1] }) (5. Ka4 { King to a4 is one move the race cannot afford. } 5... h2 6. Kb5 Kf6 7. Kxb6 h1=Q { Lost: two king moves to take his b pawn, and his new queen on h1 arrived first. [%csl Rh1] }) 5... h2 { His pawn reaches h2. } 6. a8=Q { A new queen on a8, and she guards h1 down the long diagonal, so his pawn cannot queen safely. The right column won the race. [%cal Ga7a8,Ga8h1] } (6. Kc4 { King to c4, with the queen one step away. } 6... h1=Q 7. Kb5 Qa8 8. Kxb6 Kh6 { Lost: his queen on h1 came first and then blocked a8 before your pawn could promote. [%csl Ra8] }) 1-0


[Event "Capablanca endings: Bring the king up to the majority"]
