{ His rook checks from g6, and your pawn on a7 is one step from a queen. Find the answer. } 61. Kf5 { Your king steps up and attacks the rook on g6. It must run or be guarded, and the pawn still threatens a8. [%tail][%cal Ge6f5] } (61. Kd5 { King to d5 attacks nothing. } 61... Rg5+ 62. Kc6 Rxa5 63. Kb7 Kd8 { Drawn: his rook checked on g5 and then took your rook on a5, and his king is close enough to your pawn. [%csl Ra5] }) (61. Ke5 { King to e5 walks into another check. } 61... Rg5+ 62. Kd6 Rxa5 63. Kc6 Rxa7 { Lost: his rook took your rook on a5 and then your pawn on a7, and you have a bare king. [%csl Ra7] }) 61... Kf7 62. a8=Q { A new queen on a8, against his lone rook: a win. Your king answered the check with an attack, and his rook had no time to stop the pawn. [%csl Ga8] } 1-0


